# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Restart `npm run dev` after editing —
# Vite inlines these at build time, so a running dev server will not pick up a change.
#
# For the deployed site the same variable comes from a GitHub repo secret, read by
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml. Set it under Settings → Secrets and variables →
# Actions → New repository secret, using the exact name below.
#
# Everything here is inlined into the JS bundle and visible to anyone who views
# source, which is what the PUBLIC_ prefix says. Never put a real secret here: an
# SMTP password, an API key that can spend money, a Turnstile *secret* key. Those
# belong in the Web3Forms dashboard, which is a server.

# Web3Forms access key — where the contact form delivers.
# Get one free at https://web3forms.com: enter dylannagel05@gmail.com, confirm the
# email, and paste the key it gives you here. Without it the form renders an
# honest "delivery is not configured" state and sends nothing.
#
# This key is a routing identifier, not a credential: it means "deliver to this
# inbox" and cannot read past submissions or change the destination. It can be
# scraped and POSTed to by a bot, which is what the honeypot and (once configured)
# Turnstile are for. See src/lib/contact.ts.
PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
